  "caption": "Captain Quinn set sail, born for the sea. Then came hiking out over the side (thighs on fire) and a winch that pulled harder than Quinn did.\n\nHiking postures, sudden sheet and winch loads, a moving deck and the odd boom can strain backs, knees, shoulders, elbows, hands and necks. Sore isn't simply part of sailing — your body can be trained for it.\n\nWhat can help: trunk and hip endurance like side planks, quad endurance for hiking, pulling and rotator cuff strength for winching, grip and balance work on land, plus gloves, good winch technique and plenty of water on sunny days.\n\nGet a head knock from the boom or a fall checked promptly, and get lingering elbow pain assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
